<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (     The United Nations Security Council serves as the world's most vital international authority for maintaining global peace and security. It has proven indispensable since its configuration in 1945 following World War II, seeing that it is the only international organ empowered to issue legally binding resolutions obliging all UN member states \(United Nations, 1945\). The Council holds exclusive authority to impose sanctions, approve peacekeeping operations, and authorize the use of force. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
