/Title (Today, the rise of PMCs and proxy groups continues to contradict international law, particularly state sovereignty and state responsibility. When violence is carried out through private contractors or externally backed militias, who is then responsible for violations of international humanitarian law \(International Commission of Jurists, 2019\)? As these challenges grow, the question facing the international community is no longer whether these actors exist, but how the Security Council can respond to their expanding role in contemporary warfare.)
